  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Federation University Australia has a deep history dating back to 1870, starting as the School of Mines Ballarat. Today, it is a leading regional university known for its supportive \"small-uni\" values while maintaining the reach of a large institution. The university is a top choice for students seeking a hands-on approach to learning and has earned a five-star rating for teaching quality and student support.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At Federation, you are more than just a number; you are part of a close-knit community. You can join various student groups and organisations that help you find your people and settle into Australian life. The university provides extensive support services, including dedicated help for international students to navigate their study journey and career aspirations.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Living on campus at Federation is designed to be stress‑free and social, with residences at Ballarat, Berwick, and Gippsland offering short commutes, 24/7 support, and a choice of self‑contained apartments or shared units. Weekly rent typically covers utilities and internet for easy budgeting, while students can also explore private rentals in nearby regional areas through the university’s Fedliving focus.</p><p><i>If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p>1. <strong>Library</strong></p><p>Each campus features a library designed for easy studying, providing access to computers, physical and digital learning materials, and quiet group work areas.</p><p><strong>2. Sports</strong></p><p>You can stay active with on-campus sporting facilities, including fitness centres, pools (at specific locations), and walking tracks.</p><p><strong>3. Laboratories</strong></p><p>The university boasts modern infrastructure with state-of-the-art laboratories and research facilities, including the Science and Engineering Building.</p><p><strong>4. Cafeteria</strong></p><p>You can grab a meal or coffee at on-campus spots like the <strong>Dhanda Napan Café</strong> in Gippsland or <strong>Dhanga Café</strong> in Berwick, which serve healthy meals and snacks.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
